 "The London Hammer is an iron-and-wood hammer said to have been found in Cretaceous limestone concretion near London, Texas, in 1936 (reported widely decades later). Young-Earth and OOPArt advocates call it a human tool sealed in ancient rock. Geologists note that mineral concretions can enclose recent objects, and the hammer\'s style matches 19th-century tools—so the find does not demonstrate humans in the Cretaceous.",
